{"title":"N-squared plus 1 conjecture","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The <b>n-squared plus 1 conjecture</b> is a famous conjecture in <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Number_theory\" title=\"Number theory\">Number theory</a>. It is one of the four great unsolved conjectures in <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Number_Theory\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Number Theory\">Number Theory</a> collectively known as <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Landau%27s_Problems\" title=\"Landau&#39;s Problems\">Landau's Problems</a>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Statement\">Statement</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=N-squared_plus_1_conjecture&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Statement\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are infinitely many primes in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/5/0f55a7827b23d850bed0d0c3bf0880b27ffcca2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"16\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is a positive integer.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=N-squared_plus_1_conjecture&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Goldbach_Conjecture\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Goldbach Conjecture\">Goldbach Conjecture</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Twin_Prime_Conjecture\" title=\"Twin Prime Conjecture\">Twin Prime Conjecture</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Legendre_Conjecture\" title=\"Legendre Conjecture\">Legendre Conjecture</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Landau%27s_Problems\" title=\"Landau&#39;s Problems\">Landau's Problems</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=N-squared_plus_1_conjecture&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018100927\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.010 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.015 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 25/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 322/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 346/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.267      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.267      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:30402:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018100927 and revision id 238215. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}